{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/923572-the-lunar-curse-freedom-at-any-cost","id":923572,"title":"The Lunar Curse - Freedom At Any Cost","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-29T16:59:07-07:00","id":923572,"title":"The Lunar Curse - Freedom At Any Cost","content":"<b><u>The Lunar Exalted</u> (page 46)</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Chosen of the moon were forged in the chains of bondage, but Luna only chooses those with the power to free themselves. Like the moon, they represent a struggle against form and definition, and a primal connection to the unfinished world. They wear the stolen forms of their foes. They bravely walk the tattered edges of Creation, where horrors tread. But they remain caught on the fangs of the past, and until they escape it, they cannot truly claim the freedom Luna has promised them.<br /> <br /> Though they may live as legendary thieves, peerless hunters, opulent scavenger princes, terrible living gods, seekers of the world\u2019s secrets, bloody-handed warlords, and more, all Lunars feel the weight of the past.<br /> <br /> Once the Lunars were the guardians of the Old Realm, matching their specialized guile to the raw magnificence of their Solar lords and spouses. That time ended in blood and flames, and now the Lunars wage a crusade against those who stole the world that was theirs to protect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Broken Bonds</b><br /> The Lunar Exalted were created to be the Solars\u2019 seconds, their spouses, and the sacred guardians of the Old Realm. The bond defined the Lunars; it sang within their very Essence.<br /> <br /> So too did the bond\u2019s destruction. The Old Realm fell; the Solars were murdered, their spirits banished beyond Lunar ken. The Lunars changed. They\u2019re still changing. A deep rage lives in their Essence, and a deep wound. Their sleep is tormented by visions of loss, of murder, of the past. The Lunars are compelled to shatter the chains binding them to the past\u2014to tear down the stolen remnants of the First Age, to raze the Sidereal and Terrestrial hegemony that dares to wear the ancient name of the Realm. The Silver Pact exists to facilitate this.<br /> <br /> Some Lunars resist the primal howl that shivers in their Essence. They harness their rage to fight for that which they cherish, or bend their powerful instincts to their own benefit as they walk another road. There is tension between these Lunars and the Silver Pact traditionalists, but also common bonds; the two trade favors and mark debts more often than they shed one another\u2019s blood.<br /> <br /> The return of the Solars changes everything for Luna\u2019s Chosen. Neither Lunar camp seeks to turn back the clock, nor wishes to return to defining themselves as the shadows cast by the Chosen of the sun. Something stirs in the Lunars\u2019 hearts, but none can yet say what it is or what it means.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted are afraid of the Solar Exalted re-establishing the old status quo between their hosts.<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted should be just as afraid of doing so. There was a REASON why the Usurpation happened despite the presence of their Lunar Mates, and why the First Age got so bad in the first place.<br /> <br /> Even before the Solar Exalted were murdered and cast into a mysterious darkness; even before the Lunar Exalted were chased beyond the edges of the world; even before their betrayers spat on the Realm the Lunar Exalted helped to create by daring to steal its name and Sword...<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted have been grappling with desire for freedom and the fear of entrapment ever since the Neverborn first hurled their Great Curse at the gods.<br /> <br /> Naturally, being haunted by unbreakable emotional attachments and hunted for the crime of existing has only made things worse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>The Rattling of Shattered Manacles</b></u><br /> The Lunar Exalted gain and lose Limit in the same ways as the Solar Exalted, with one slight exception. A Lunar Exalt's Limit Trigger is determined by the specific sort of &quot;chain&quot; that they gained Luna's approval by breaking; when the Lunar is confronted by that situation or observes someone she cares about suffering the same fate. Here is a list of examples:<br /> <br /> * The Lunar is forced to flee or fight (or beg) for her life.<br /> <br /> * The Lunar is bodily crippled, physically bound, incarcerated, or otherwise compelled to remain in some place against her desires.<br /> <br /> * The Lunar falls ill with disease or poison.<br /> <br /> * The Lunar incurs any penalty from deprivation of sleep, food, water, or air.<br /> <br /> * The Lunar becomes seriously indebted to another character, or else subjected to serious blackmail.<br /> <br /> * The Lunar is tempted to partake in a vice to which she was once addicted, or for which she is trying to break an addiction.<br /> <br /> * The Lunar is betrayed by someone for whom she holds a positive Tie.<br /> <br /> * The Lunar is denied an opportunity to advance her own interests because of some legal custom or social more.<br /> <br /> * The Lunar suffers a serious loss in material resources or is denied an opportunity to advance her own interests because of the risk of suffering a serious material loss.<br /> <br /> * The Lunar's allies suffer a setback or defeat because of a mistake she made.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Freedom Flaws</b></u><br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted share the <b>Berserk Anger</b> and <b>Rampaging Avarice</b> Flaws with the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Iconoclasm</b></i><br /> The Lunar seeks out the most important physical representation of a particular social group, and destroys it without regard for the consequences. This may include murdering <i>living </i>representatives.<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> Session. Iconoclasm can only be ended prematurely if the Lunar sees how her actions to fulfill her manic goal are hurting or threatening her loved ones; this does not include the consequences of fulfilling the goal itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Turnabout Is Fair Play</b></i><br /> The Lunar allies herself with her loved one's enemies, seeking to advance their goals at the expense of his. She will divulge any of his secrets that don't also threaten her own interests.<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene. Turnabout Is Fair Play can only be ended prematurely if the Lunar sees how her actions are hurting a different loved one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Slavish Devotion</b></i><br /> The Lunar abdicates all personal responsibility or agency, declaring herself the servant of a loved one in order to earn or win back his approval or forgiveness.<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene. Slavish Devotion can be ended prematurely if the Lunar is forced to face a significant challenge alone and succeeds, or if she is forgiven by the character to whom she devoted herself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Run And Hide</b></i><br /> Overcome with fear -- of social censure, death, or causing harm to her loved ones -- the Lunar Exalt attempts to flee the scene and hide, in no particular order. She will attack anyone who chases her out of hiding or who attempts to keep her from escaping, though if the one is someone she loves, she will attempt to repel them without serious injury and will not place her freedom above their life and limb.<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene. Run And Hide can be ended prematurely if leaving the scene would put one of the Lunar's loved ones in immediate danger. The Storyteller should obviously avoid choosing this Flaw in situations where the Lunar would immediately break free of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Bare Necessities (Ascetic Drive)</b></i><br /> Confronted by the tyranny of owning too many things that one fears to lose, the character casts aside the possessions that possess her. She destroys her worldly goods or else leaves them to those she loves or trusts, dresses as simply or minimally as feasible, and seeks enlightenment and meditation through exercise and self-reflection.<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> One full day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Identity Dissociation</b></i><br /> Unable to look herself in the mirror, the Lunar forgets herself and convinces herself that she is someone entirely different. Lunar Exalted often end up adopting the identities of people whose heart's blood they stole, which usually means unwittingly advancing the goals of an enemy. One memorable, cautionary tale among Luna's Chosen is the Exalt who assumed the identity of a Dragon-Blood, realized &quot;he&quot; was actually the Anathema who murdered and ate him, and then killed &quot;himself&quot; in revenge.<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> Until the character next sleeps; when she wakes up, she will remember who she is, but she will not remember what she did during her Limit Break without memory-retrieving magic, even when confronted by evidence and eye-witness accounts. She can be made to remember who she is prematurely only when she encounters a situation in which ignorance of her true identity puts her loved ones in danger.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Animal Simplicity</b></i><br /> As per Identity Dissociation, but the Lunar convinces herself that she is merely a stupid beast, without any capacity for higher thought. The Lunar needn't fear working towards an enemies goals in her forgetfulness, but she can find herself in all sorts of trouble that a mere animal couldn't think to avoid.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Short-Term Amnesia</i></b><br /> The most deceptively mild of Limit Breaks; the Lunar simply forgets everything that happened earlier in the scene, and then forgets the rest of the scene after it is over, acting as if it had never happened. The Lunar loses all points of Limit, but regains no Willpower.<br /> <br /> What makes this Limit Break dangerous is that it turns the Lunar into even more of a ticking time-bomb. If the Lunar should be confronted with sufficient evidence or eye-witnesses accounts of what happened, or otherwise recover her memories of that scene in any way, she flies into a brand new Limit Break. If those around her are lucky, she just suffers Short-Term Amnesia again, forgetting the original scene as well as the parts of this one related to remembering it, losing none of her current Limit points, and gaining no Willpower points.<br /> <br /> If she instead suffers a different Freedom Flaw upon remembering, she will regain Willpower as normal after it is over, but she still won't lose her current number of Limit Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-29-2016, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T13:35:44-08:00","id":1187129,"title":"","content":"Perhaps people might want to discuss this now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T18:33:02-08:00","id":1187421,"title":"","content":"I'm a little iffy about mandating relationships, bonds, and chains into the story; or about introducing unavoidable insecurities into Exalted - but I like what you've put together!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I'm spoiler tagging this part because it feels like I'm about to retype something that will be fan-forum-angst, and that isn't my intent. I just want to explain my thoughts on Lunar/Solar bond and how it's seemed to appear up to now. <br /> <br /> There seems to be a very poor place in the story for any particular group that is defined in terms of some other group. That kind of story setting seems to set up the whole group as perpetual second-fiddles to somebody better, cooler, and more important. <br /> <br /> Also, if a player tells me they want to be a terrifying monster or an iconoclastic freedom fighter, it just seems hinky to me to enforce them being somebody's wife. Not every shaggy beastman is Enkidu; If a player tells me that they want to play a character who doesn't give a hot flip about some bound reincarnation cycle love affair, I'm inclined to agree with them. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I think I'm reading too much into this, but it reads like you're setting up a range of options. <br /> <br /> On one end, you have the Lunars who embrace the bond in the style described in prior editions: the grip of the bond my be (in character) voluntary or not, and it might have benefits but also fears, mistrusts, and betrayals, which lead to Limit. For them, the worst thing might be being alone - someone must adore them or oppose them or recognize them.<br /> <br /> On the other, the Lunars who have no bond or are bond-ambivalent (<i>now you're just some Solar that I used to know</i>): They avoid limit by being free in general, but have hidden in their psyche some especially strong aversion to a particular type of &quot;chain&quot;, which leads to Limit. For them, the worst thing might be entanglements with others.<br /> <br /> If I'm reading into that correctly, you most assuredly have my interest! <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T19:26:31-08:00","id":1187432,"title":"","content":"In Third Edition, not every Lunar was spiritually bound to a Solar. For one thing, there weren't enough Solars, as the Lunar Exalted outnumber them 400-to-300.<br /> <br /> Also, this potential curse has nothing to do with the Solar Exalted or the Lunars relationships with them. It has everything to do with freedom and restrictions in general.<br /> <br /> Don't want chains or relationships? How about &quot;I refused to die when suffering from a crippling, chronic disease&quot; and then you gained your freedom when the moon goddess Chose you?<br /> <br /> <br /> In any case, this was written back when I thought &quot;bondage and freedom&quot; was going to be a universal theme for Lunar Exaltation.<br /> <br /> I bring it back up because it's idea for how to give Lunar Exalted limit breaks which are distinctly different from those of Solar Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T04:13:27-08:00","id":1187511,"title":"","content":"I like where you're going with it. I think it reinforces the idea of Lunars being something completely different. I like that it's neutral to barbarianism and being a critter person - could work with or without them.<br /> <br /> Are you tying Lunar Limit, then, to the circumstances of Exaltation? <br /> <br /> I'm intrigued by the idea of casting Limit in terms of chaining or caging the beast, and casting Limit Break to feel like freedom gone amok. (Again, possibly inferring other than what you wrote, but that's how the idea is turning over in my mind right now) <br /> <br /> Good work so far!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}